# CVE-2026-12151: undici DoS via unbounded WebSocket memory growth.
# Affected package: undici bundled inside npm's own node_modules, not in application code.
# npm is used only as a process runner (CMD ["npm", "start"]), not as an HTTP/WebSocket client.
# Exploitability: negligible — npm never opens a WebSocket in this deployment context.
CVE-2026-12151

# GHSA-f88m-g3jw-g9cj (CVE-2026-33327, CVE-2026-33328, CVE-2026-35590, CVE-2026-35591)
# libvips vulnerabilities inherited by sharp, bundled as an optionalDependency of next@16.2.x.
# next@16.2.x pins sharp@^0.34.5 — npm overrides do not apply to optionalDependencies and
# no updated Next.js release is available. sharp is used for static image optimisation only
# (not processing user-supplied data), so the attack surface is minimal.
GHSA-f88m-g3jw-g9cj
CVE-2026-33327
CVE-2026-33328
CVE-2026-35590
CVE-2026-35591

# CVE-2026-14257: brace-expansion DoS via catastrophic backtracking.
# Affected package: brace-expansion v5.0.7 bundled inside npm's own node_modules
# (usr/local/lib/node_modules/npm/node_modules/brace-expansion), not in application code.
# npm is used only as a process runner in production; brace-expansion is never invoked at
# runtime. The version is pinned by npm's own internal dependency tree (not overridable).
CVE-2026-14257

# CVE-2026-64641, CVE-2026-64642, CVE-2026-64645, CVE-2026-64649: Next.js App Router vulnerabilities.
# Affected package: next@16.2.6 (fixed in 16.2.11).
# CVE-2026-64641: DoS via Server Actions — requires Server Actions exposed to untrusted input.
# CVE-2026-64642: Middleware bypass — requires Turbopack, which is not enabled in this project.
# CVE-2026-64645: SSRF via rewrites — this application does not use rewrites with external
# destinations.
# CVE-2026-64649: SSRF in Server Actions on custom servers — this project uses Next.js standalone
# mode (not a custom server). Upgrade to next@16.2.11 is planned for the next sprint.
CVE-2026-64641
CVE-2026-64642
CVE-2026-64645
CVE-2026-64649

# CVE-2026-45623, GHSA-r28c-9q8g-f849: PostCSS file read / path traversal via sourceMappingURL.
# Affected package: postcss@8.4.31 bundled inside next@16.2.x (not a direct dependency).
# PostCSS is a build-time CSS processor; it is not executed at request time in the production
# image. CSS is compiled to static assets during `next build`; sourceMappingURL in user-supplied
# CSS is never processed at runtime. Will be resolved when next.js is upgraded to 16.2.11+.
CVE-2026-45623
GHSA-r28c-9q8g-f849
